/datum/faith/oldkin
	name = "The Old Kin"
	desc = "The everyday folk religion of Vaeltis - hearth-shrines, wood-shrines, and the barely-a-god you leave an offering for at a \
		crossroads. Trnava of the forests stands most central among them, alongside Volkovoi of the winter cull, Hausvette of the \
		harvest and hearth, and Klokner, who answers from boundaries and lost places. \n\
		The high orthodoxy of the Concordat and the Tribunal both look down on the Old Kin as superstition unworthy of a Seat or a \
		Word, but most common folk keep these shrines without contradiction alongside their civic worship: a coin left for Hausvette \
		at the hearth is no less pious than a vow sworn before a magistrate."
	worshippers = "Farmers, Foresters, Hunters, Midwives, and Commonfolk of Every Seat"
	godhead = /datum/patron/oldkin/trnava
	preference_accessible = TRUE
